  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, aEDPA contains a tolling rule for prisoners seeking to gather new evidence."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the petitioner must act quickly because adverse consequences can occur if he does not."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "If the petitioner is close to the end of his one\u2011year period, he can file a protective habeas petition, ask for a stay, and continue pursuing a new affidavit."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 7,
                "start": 7
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, filing a protective habeas petition puts the State on notice and gives it an opportunity to investigate the new evidence."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 11,
                "start": 11
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the petitioner urges the Court to address a circuit split on whether the limitations period applies."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0009"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 12,
                "start": 12
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, there are three categories of prisoners who claim actual innocence based on new evidence."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "John J. Bursch",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 65,
                "start": 65
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to John J. Bursch, the State\u2019s interest in timeliness is strongest when new evidence relates to the constitutional claim, and the petitioner seeks extraordinary tolling rather than equitable tolling."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "John J. Bursch",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 60,
                "start": 60
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to John J. Bursch, legislative silence on equitable tolling indicates Congress intended the limitations period to apply to cases involving new evidence."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "John J. Bursch",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 64,
                "start": 64
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to John J. Bursch, the successive\u2011petition provision adds an actual\u2011innocence gateway that is not available on a first petition."
        }
      ],
